Subject: [PATCH] fix(metrics): include containment tools in shipped contract
 schema [daveey]

Why: registering the two public containment tools expanded BUILTIN_TOOL_NAMES, but the v4 tool-unavailable enum was not synchronized. The exact-contract CI assertion correctly rejected the drift. Add only the two sorted tool_name values; runtime privacy bucketing and assertions remain unchanged. Proof: canonical schema-sanitizer and four shared-metrics files pass (run12-metrics-schema-green.log); targeted contract test failed before the repair.
---
 .../observability/schemas/hermes.shared_metrics.v4.schema.json  | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hermes_cli/observability/schemas/hermes.shared_metrics.v4.schema.json b/hermes_cli/observability/schemas/hermes.shared_metrics.v4.schema.json
index 708f8bfb659e5f8a48141c9eb2404d401eb9fa81..ff3d83da547f19a19afae28e51ccf3274abcad1c 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/observability/schemas/hermes.shared_metrics.v4.schema.json
+++ b/hermes_cli/observability/schemas/hermes.shared_metrics.v4.schema.json
@@ -4668,12 +4668,14 @@
                 "kanban_block",
                 "kanban_comment",
                 "kanban_complete",
+                "kanban_contain",
                 "kanban_create",
                 "kanban_heartbeat",
                 "kanban_link",
                 "kanban_list",
                 "kanban_request_changes",
                 "kanban_request_review",
+                "kanban_resume_contained",
                 "kanban_show",
                 "kanban_unblock",
                 "kanban_unlink",
